> tl;dr
>
> - ~58 hours/month reclaimed across 48 active editors (~1.2 h each) via Release 5.11.
> - Editor menu performance improved ~20% (7.8s → 6.18s).
> - Standardized publication cover workflow cut steps from 9 to 3.
> - Results delivered by a cross‑functional team (engineering, design, content ops) under clear leadership and governance.

No single issue was breaking the editorial experience—but the accumulation of paper cuts was slowing everything down. The site felt sluggish. Navigation was slow. Saving content would occasionally time out. The editor menu took 7+ seconds to load. None of these problems were catastrophic on their own, but together they were draining editor time and patience.

We dedicated time in our 3-week release cycle to address this backlog of friction. We introduced a new menu concept, fixed underlying performance bugs, automated repetitive workflows, and optimized database queries. The kind of work that's easy to defer when there's always a "more important" feature—but the cumulative impact was significant.

We measured this rigorously: 48 active editors, the frequency of common tasks (publications, news items, updates), and the time each task required. When we multiplied task frequency × time saved × editor count, the result was ~58 hours reclaimed per month. Not from one heroic fix, but from addressing a dozen small sources of friction.

## Problem

Fragmented editorial steps and inconsistent tooling increased time‑to‑publish and human error, reducing capacity for strategic content work.

## Approach

- Standardized Drupal CMS workflows across presences via the Public Web Platform.
- Automated PDF cover image generation and image crops for publications.
- Optimized editor navigation and UI performance.

### Before → After (publication covers)

- Before: 9 steps (create entry, open Photoshop, crop, save, create media, upload, name, specify 6 crops, select image).
- After: 3 steps (create entry, system auto‑generates cover, optionally override).

## Outcomes (averaged over typical month)

- Publications: 166 items × ~10 minutes saved ≈ ~27 hours saved.
- Other items: 377 entries × ~5 minutes saved ≈ ~31 hours saved.
- Total estimated time reclaimed: ~58 hours/month (≈ 1.5 work weeks).
- Per‑editor average: ~50 minutes saved/week.
- Editor UI speed: ~20% faster (7.8s → 6.18s).

